              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "dēspondeō, dēspondēre — \"to promise in marriage, to betroth\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Pater fīliam suam amīcō dēspondit. The father promised his daughter in marriage to a friend."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "dēspondeō, dēspondēre, dēspondī, dēspōnsum. Animum dēspondēre: to lose heart, which gives English despond."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "dēspondeō is built on spondeō, \"to promise solemnly\", with dē- (EtymDB): to promise away. English despond comes from its use with animum, \"to lose heart\"."
            }
          ]
        },
